c/sensei_top/logs.py`:\n\n- **New `_Level` filter**, next to `_Session`. It passes records at or above its floor. Below the floor it passes only INFO and up from `sensei_top.llm` or a name starting with `sensei_top.llm.`, so `sensei_top.llmx` stays out.\n- **Console handler** is set to INFO, with `_Level(WARNING)` under `--verbose` and `_Level(ERROR)` otherwise.\n- **File handler** is set to DEBUG under `--verbose` and INFO otherwise. Without `--verbose`, a `_Level(WARNING)` filter goes on after the header is written, so the INFO header still gets through.\n- **Module docstring** \"Levels\" bullet now says both handlers also take `sensei_top.llm`'s INFO lines.\n\nI did not run the full test suite, the dashboard checks, or the end-to-end ingest/project/report check, since the spec only lists these two commands. I did not commit anything.", "ttft_ms": 1810, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 16637, "uuid": "2f1e3ff8-f6d9-4a3d-85e7-21e03fe320ce", "ttft_stream_ms": 1650, "time_to_request_ms": 444, "first_content_frame_ms": 1650, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
